ce* of how early humans survived, and how we should *actually behave* in the woods today. Looking back at history, it's fascinating to realize that our ancestors survived through trial, error, and a lot of stomachaches. But looking forward at how we should act today? You are spot on. Treating every unknown plant as a deadly threat is the smartest, safest, and most logical way to approach the wild. Your parents taught you well!
